{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":243156,"num_turns":31,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"467b8c2e-1551-45b1-bac2-82999c7910fa","total_cost_usd":0.8633807999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":109586,"cache_read_input_tokens":1066184,"output_tokens":20937,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11840},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":109586,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10314,"cache_read_input_tokens":108618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":968},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2305,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00237,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":30,"outputTokens":20937,"cacheReadInputTokens":1066184,"cacheCreationInputTokens":109586,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8610107999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"architecture_summary\":\"A deterministic local \\\"supervisor\\\" (never fully built) is meant to own an autonomous loop: GDD canon -> persistent Tasks/*.yaml work graph -> progressive decomposition -> bounded single-agent execution through a provider-neutral AgentRuntime -> GER-style implement/evaluate/refine -> Git/Unity evidence -> human merge -> conformance re-evaluation. As of the frozen commit, only the governance/audit skeleton is real: a 37-record task-contract graph (schema 2.0, mutable status removed), a Git-object-level evidence/conformance evaluator (Phase 3A), a fail-closed AgentRuntime with Claude and Codex read-only provider adapters, and an eight-reviewer ArchitectureReview tool migrated onto that runtime. Dispatch/readiness/authorization are all hard-coded to deny (`taskcontrol ready` -> UNAVAILABLE, `taskcontrol authorize` -> DENIED), no ExecutionCrew exists, and neither provider adapter supports repository writing. Exactly one task (NSC-023, the isometric camera) has real conformance evidence, and that evidence was hand-authored after the feature was built outside the pipeline (via Assignment 6 coursework), not delivered through AgentRuntime/TaskExecution.\",\"overall_verdict\":\"sound_overbuilt\",\"verdict_reason\":\"The core instincts are correct and evidence-grounded: don't let a model self-certify completion, keep dependency/readiness computation deterministic, treat runtime Unity evidence as first-class (Assignment 6's camera lesson), and don't let mutable task metadata substitute for proof (the Phase 1-3 correction directly fixed a real defect the prior architecture review found). But the team has now spent five staged commits (4A-4D) building elaborate provider-transport and evidence-integrity machinery for a tool that reviews the pipeline itself, while the two capabilities actually required to produce game-development leverage — (1) any provider capability to write code, and (2) any deterministic/cheap way to propagate a GDD edit into the living Tasks/*.yaml graph — remain entirely unbuilt. The project's own CURRENT_STATE.md promises a \\\"taskcontrol reconciliation-diff/apply workflow\\\" to own GDD-driven graph changes \\\"in Milestone 1,\\\" but Milestone 1 is marked complete and no such command exists in taskcontrol.py. Given the explicit premise that the GDD is iterative, this is not a hypothetical gap — it's a load-bearing piece of the design that was described but never implemented, while adjacent, lower-priority machinery (dual-provider comparison scaffolding, Git-blob-level artifact integrity checks, malformed-JSON adversarial hardening) received heavy investment despite zero production incidents to justify their priority. This is overbuilding in the wrong order, not a wrong architecture.\",\"strong_decisions\":[\"ADR-002/ADR-007/Phase 1-3: mutable task status cannot authorize execution; completion is evidence-derived from committed Git state, not a worker's self-report — this directly fixed a real defect the prior review surfaced.\",\"Fail-closed dispatch: taskcontrol ready/authorize are hard-denied until a real dependency-readiness and dispatch policy exists, rather than quietly enabling autonomy prematurely.\",\"current_conformance.py reads only committed HEAD, explicitly ignoring uncommitted working-tree evidence (demonstrated live: NSC-023 flipped from not_delivered to conformant only after the evidence was committed).\",\"Runtime evidence as first-class validation input (ADR-015), motivated by the real Assignment 6 finding that the camera passed static evaluation while being unusable at runtime.\",\"Reconciliation snapshots are immutable and never directly rewrite Tasks/*.yaml (ADR-025/026) — protects the living graph from uncontrolled LLM-driven cascading edits.\",\"Provider adapters are fail-closed on capability, budget, and schema shape (ClaudeCodeProvider rejects repository_write/approved_command_execution, non-null token_limit, unsupported models) rather than silently degrading.\"],\"structural_flaws\":[\"No GDD-to-living-graph synchronization tool exists despite being explicitly promised: Pipeline/Reconciliation/README.md states a 'deterministic taskcontrol reconciliation-diff/apply workflow' will own comparing new reconciliation output against Tasks/*.yaml, but taskcontrol.py's subparsers only contain validate/list/show/ready/authorize/state/graph — no diff or apply command exists anywhere in the repo.\",\"GDD staleness detection only fires for tasks that already have a committed evidence record (current_conformance.py compares canon['sha256'] against current_canon_hash inside the record-evaluation loop). The other ~36 of 37 task contracts have no evidence yet, so a GDD edit that invalidates their acceptance criteria produces zero signal until someone manually reruns full reconciliation and manually diffs 37 files by hand.\",\"Neither live provider adapter (Claude or Codex) supports repository_write or approved_command_execution — the elaborate AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack cannot currently make a single Unity code change, autonomously or semi-autonomously.\",\"Evidence records require hand-authored JSON with exact Git blob SHA-256 values per conformance surface and gate artifact (CONFORMANCE_RECORDS.md), but no generator/authoring tool exists in Pipeline/TaskGraph — only a validator/reader (conformance_records.py exposes shape validation and load_committed_records, nothing that computes and writes a record).\",\"The project's own accepted correction direction (CURRENT_STATE.md, 'Deferred Until Evidence Justifies It') explicitly warns against building infrastructure ahead of a proven single delivery loop, yet the five most recent commits (Stage 4A-4D) are all infrastructure for ArchitectureReview provider migration, not gameplay work — the project is not currently following its own stated rule.\"],\"observed_failure_solutions\":[\"Prior architecture review found mutable task 'status' was being treated as completion truth; Phase 1-3 replaced it with schema-2.0 contracts plus a separate evidence-derived conformance evaluator that reads only committed Git state.\",\"Assignment 6 found a Refiner could report 'implemented' while making no actual file changes; ADR-016 makes a no-op refinement count as a failed repair attempt against budget.\",\"Assignment 6 found static/source-level evaluation passed while the camera was unusable at runtime; ADR-015 makes runtime Unity evidence able to fail a task even after static evaluation passes.\",\"An early Phase 3A test found uncommitted evidence could be mistaken for proof; the evaluator was built/verified to ignore working-tree state and only trust committed HEAD (demonstrated concretely with NSC-023).\"],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[\"Extensive provider trust-boundary adversarial hardening (malformed/duplicate JSON keys, NaN/Infinity rejection, path traversal in raw_log_reference, provider identity mismatch checks) defends against attacks that have not occurred in this single-user, offline, Docker-contained environment.\",\"Git-blob-SHA-level integrity checking on every conformance surface and gate-artifact evidence record defends against evidence tampering that has never been observed and is unlikely given ADR-038's accepted single-trusted-user boundary.\",\"Dual-provider (Claude vs Codex) architecture-review scaffolding, provider namespace separation, and 'later comparison' plumbing were built with 'no comparison pipeline exists yet' explicitly acknowledged — infrastructure for a feature that doesn't exist and has no scheduled owner.\",\"ADR-027's two-different-model bootstrap verification requirement and the parallel multi-model verification crew (opus+sonnet, randomized model assignment, union-not-vote findings) is heavy machinery for a one-time 37-record bootstrap that has already happened and is marked 'do not rerun.'\"],\"overengineering\":[\"Stage 4A-4D provider-adapter migration effort (turn-budget translation formulas, StandardProcessRunner, capability-mapping ADRs, provider registry identity checks) was spent entirely on migrating the ArchitectureReview meta-tool, which produces no game content and was already functional before the migration.\",\"The evidence-record schema (delivery/baseline/revalidation with basis-chain ancestry cycle detection, Git blob SHA binding for every surface and artifact) is more rigorous than anything needed to prove one prototype scene works, and currently has no authoring tool, making it a burden rather than leverage for the next real task.\",\"Immutable per-run reconciliation/verification directory trees with nested pass1/pass2/stream_repairs/MODEL_ASSIGNMENTS artifacts represent significant process ceremony for a single 37-item bootstrap that ran once.\"],\"missing_components\":[\"A GDD-change-to-task-contract impact/diff tool (promised, never built).\",\"Any tool to author Phase 3A evidence records (compute Git blob SHAs, assemble the JSON) instead of hand-writing them.\",\"Repository write capability in any provider adapter — without this, AgentRuntime cannot be used to implement anything.\",\"ExecutionCrew (Planner/Implementer/Validator wired to AgentRuntime) — Assignment 3's crew and Assignment 6's GER loop remain isolated coursework, never integrated into the production runtime.\",\"A cheap, per-task GDD-chunk hash/version binding at the task-contract level (contracts store free-text gdd_evidence references but no hash), so drift can only be detected after evidence already exists.\"],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"AgentRuntime/TaskExecution separation (ADR-039) is a reasonable boundary in principle but currently guards a system with no real task-execution consumer; the split's value is unproven.\",\"Tasks/*.yaml is declared 'approved definition of work, not completion truth,' and Phase 3A evidence is declared the completion authority — this two-tier model is coherent, but there is no defined authority for a third state that will matter constantly under an iterative GDD: 'this approved task definition may now be wrong because canon changed underneath it before any evidence was ever recorded.' Nothing owns that question today.\",\"Reconciliation is correctly kept from directly mutating the graph, but because the promised diff/apply boundary doesn't exist, there is currently no path at all — not even a manual one with tool support — from a new reconciliation snapshot into the living graph after bootstrap.\"],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"The architecture treats GDD sync as binary: either nothing happens (silent drift) or a full multi-model reconciliation + verification crew re-runs (the same heavyweight bootstrap machinery), with no built middle tier for 'this one paragraph changed, which 2 tasks does it touch.'\",\"Staleness detection is evidence-record-scoped, not contract-scoped, so the 36 of 37 tasks without evidence get no automated signal when GDD text they depend on changes.\",\"CURRENT_STATE.md explicitly defers 'automatic GDD impact analysis without a reviewed causal model' to 'later candidates driven by observed production needs' — but the prompt's premise (GDD will keep changing while the game is built) makes this a near-certain near-term need, not a speculative one; deferring it risks accumulating undetected canon drift across most of the graph.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"Zero gameplay features have been delivered through the pipeline's own machinery. The only Unity code that exists (15 C# files under one DoorPrototype scene: camera, door interaction, mana, health, WASD movement) was built directly by a human/Assignment coursework, not via AgentRuntime/TaskExecution/ExecutionCrew — none of which can currently write code at all. The one conformance proof (NSC-023) is a retrofit of pre-existing work into the new evidence schema, not a demonstration of the pipeline producing new work. All claimed leverage is still theoretical.\",\"human_intervention_points\":[\"Every reconciliation bootstrap and future reconciliation delta requires human approval before seeding/changing the graph.\",\"NSC-003 cannot proceed without a human first resolving input-ownership/arbitration questions (click-to-move vs held-pointer, suspend/reset semantics) that CURRENT_STATE.md lists as open.\",\"Every Phase 3A evidence record currently requires a human to hand-author JSON with exact Git blob SHAs (no tool exists).\",\"Every task remains permanently gated by taskcontrol authorize returning DENIED — a human must manually drive every step of every task indefinitely under current policy.\",\"Human Play Mode approval was required and recorded for NSC-023's only real conformance proof.\"],\"next_slice\":{\"title\":\"Execute exactly one small NSC-003-derived gameplay slice by hand-in-the-loop with Claude, and build only the evidence-authoring tool this exposes as missing\",\"why\":\"The architecture has never been exercised end-to-end on new work. The single highest-value experiment is not more AgentRuntime/provider plumbing but proving (or disproving) that the existing evidence/conformance model is usable in practice for a real, small, human-supervised delivery, since the pipeline cannot yet write code autonomously anyway.\",\"deliverables\":[\"Human resolves the NSC-003 input-ownership questions already listed in CURRENT_STATE.md and, if warranted, splits NSC-003 into a smaller first contract (e.g. just the shared pointer-projection foundation).\",\"Implement that one small piece directly with Claude Code (interactive, human-supervised, no AgentRuntime dependency since write capability doesn't exist) and get it merged to main with Unity Play Mode evidence.\",\"Build a minimal script (e.g. `taskcontrol record`) that computes Git blob SHAs and writes a schema-valid delivery/baseline evidence record instead of hand-authoring JSON.\",\"Run `taskcontrol state` to prove the new task flips to conformant, and note exactly what broke or was missing along the way.\"],\"proof_of_value\":\"A second real task (beyond NSC-023) reaches 'conformant' through the evidence model with materially less manual JSON authoring than today, and the exercise produces a concrete, evidence-based list of what ExecutionCrew/AgentRuntime write-capability work is actually needed next — rather than more speculative provider/transport investment.\"},\"do_not_build_yet\":[\"ExecutionCrew role orchestration or any autonomous dispatch/readiness policy.\",\"Repository-write capability for provider adapters until at least one human-supervised task has proven the evidence loop end-to-end by hand.\",\"Dual-provider (Claude vs Codex) comparison pipeline.\",\"Milestone 2's full RAG/Scanner/Progressive-Decomposer/Artifact-Authority bundle as one platform — the project's own CURRENT_STATE.md already reaches this conclusion and it should be honored, not just documented.\",\"Any further ArchitectureReview/AgentRuntime provider-migration refactoring; this tooling already works and does not block game progress.\"],\"alternative_architecture\":{\"needed\":false,\"description\":\"The state/authority shape (deterministic graph, evidence-derived conformance, immutable audit trail, human merge gate, bounded worker) does not need to be replaced. If anything, a leaner version would drop the multi-provider transport abstraction and Git-blob-level evidence integrity until a single provider has actually delivered several real tasks through it.\",\"why_better\":\"Not applicable — replacement is not warranted; the fix is sequencing (build write capability and lightweight GDD-drift detection before further governance hardening), not a different architecture.\"},\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md\",\"observation\":\"taskcontrol ready is hard-coded UNAVAILABLE and authorize is DENIED; no gameplay task has passed through the pipeline; ExecutionCrew, dependency readiness, and dispatch remain unimplemented.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py\",\"observation\":\"build_parser only registers validate/list/show/ready/authorize/state/graph subcommands; no diff or apply command exists despite Reconciliation/README.md promising one.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/Reconciliation/README.md\",\"observation\":\"States a 'deterministic taskcontrol reconciliation-diff/apply workflow will own that comparison in Milestone 1,' but Milestone 1 is marked complete and this tool was never built.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py\",\"observation\":\"GDD/canon staleness (needs_revalidation) is only checked inside the per-record evaluation loop, so contracts without any evidence record get no staleness signal at all.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/claude_code.py\",\"observation\":\"_validate_request_policy rejects repository_write and approved_command_execution outright; the provider can only read/search, never write code.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskExecution/README.md\",\"observation\":\"TaskExecution only publishes audit data and delegates to AgentRuntime; explicitly states it does not establish delivery, readiness, authorization, or completion, and ExecutionCrew remains outside this layer.\"},{\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/CONFORMANCE_RECORDS.md and conformance_records.py\",\"observation\":\"Evidence records require hand-specified Git blob SHA-256 values per surface/artifact; conformance_records.py exposes only shape validation/loading, no authoring tool.\"},{\"path\":\"Glob: Assets/**/*.cs vs Pipeline infra tree\",\"observation\":\"Only 15 gameplay C# files exist (one DoorPrototype scene) versus dozens of Python modules across TaskGraph, AgentRuntime, Reconciliation, ArchitectureReview, and TaskExecution.\"},{\"path\":\"Docs/AI-Pipeline/START_HERE.md\",\"observation\":\"'The next infrastructure work should also advance a real No Safe Circle task rather than creating another infrastructure-only stretch' — yet the five most recent commits (Stage 4A-4D) are ArchitectureReview provider migration, not gameplay work.\"}],\"confidence\":0.72,\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"Whether the team intends the very next session (post-checkpoint) to pivot hard into executing NSC-003-derived work by hand, which would resolve most of my throughput concerns quickly, or whether momentum will continue toward further AgentRuntime/ExecutionCrew infrastructure (e.g., adding write capability, building ExecutionCrew) before any second real task is proven through the evidence model — I could not observe intent beyond the frozen commit.\"}","structured_output":{"architecture_summary":"A deterministic local \"supervisor\" (never fully built) is meant to own an autonomous loop: GDD canon -> persistent Tasks/*.yaml work graph -> progressive decomposition -> bounded single-agent execution through a provider-neutral AgentRuntime -> GER-style implement/evaluate/refine -> Git/Unity evidence -> human merge -> conformance re-evaluation. As of the frozen commit, only the governance/audit skeleton is real: a 37-record task-contract graph (schema 2.0, mutable status removed), a Git-object-level evidence/conformance evaluator (Phase 3A), a fail-closed AgentRuntime with Claude and Codex read-only provider adapters, and an eight-reviewer ArchitectureReview tool migrated onto that runtime. Dispatch/readiness/authorization are all hard-coded to deny (`taskcontrol ready` -> UNAVAILABLE, `taskcontrol authorize` -> DENIED), no ExecutionCrew exists, and neither provider adapter supports repository writing. Exactly one task (NSC-023, the isometric camera) has real conformance evidence, and that evidence was hand-authored after the feature was built outside the pipeline (via Assignment 6 coursework), not delivered through AgentRuntime/TaskExecution.","overall_verdict":"sound_overbuilt","verdict_reason":"The core instincts are correct and evidence-grounded: don't let a model self-certify completion, keep dependency/readiness computation deterministic, treat runtime Unity evidence as first-class (Assignment 6's camera lesson), and don't let mutable task metadata substitute for proof (the Phase 1-3 correction directly fixed a real defect the prior architecture review found). But the team has now spent five staged commits (4A-4D) building elaborate provider-transport and evidence-integrity machinery for a tool that reviews the pipeline itself, while the two capabilities actually required to produce game-development leverage — (1) any provider capability to write code, and (2) any deterministic/cheap way to propagate a GDD edit into the living Tasks/*.yaml graph — remain entirely unbuilt. The project's own CURRENT_STATE.md promises a \"taskcontrol reconciliation-diff/apply workflow\" to own GDD-driven graph changes \"in Milestone 1,\" but Milestone 1 is marked complete and no such command exists in taskcontrol.py. Given the explicit premise that the GDD is iterative, this is not a hypothetical gap — it's a load-bearing piece of the design that was described but never implemented, while adjacent, lower-priority machinery (dual-provider comparison scaffolding, Git-blob-level artifact integrity checks, malformed-JSON adversarial hardening) received heavy investment despite zero production incidents to justify their priority. This is overbuilding in the wrong order, not a wrong architecture.","strong_decisions":["ADR-002/ADR-007/Phase 1-3: mutable task status cannot authorize execution; completion is evidence-derived from committed Git state, not a worker's self-report — this directly fixed a real defect the prior review surfaced.","Fail-closed dispatch: taskcontrol ready/authorize are hard-denied until a real dependency-readiness and dispatch policy exists, rather than quietly enabling autonomy prematurely.","current_conformance.py reads only committed HEAD, explicitly ignoring uncommitted working-tree evidence (demonstrated live: NSC-023 flipped from not_delivered to conformant only after the evidence was committed).","Runtime evidence as first-class validation input (ADR-015), motivated by the real Assignment 6 finding that the camera passed static evaluation while being unusable at runtime.","Reconciliation snapshots are immutable and never directly rewrite Tasks/*.yaml (ADR-025/026) — protects the living graph from uncontrolled LLM-driven cascading edits.","Provider adapters are fail-closed on capability, budget, and schema shape (ClaudeCodeProvider rejects repository_write/approved_command_execution, non-null token_limit, unsupported models) rather than silently degrading."],"structural_flaws":["No GDD-to-living-graph synchronization tool exists despite being explicitly promised: Pipeline/Reconciliation/README.md states a 'deterministic taskcontrol reconciliation-diff/apply workflow' will own comparing new reconciliation output against Tasks/*.yaml, but taskcontrol.py's subparsers only contain validate/list/show/ready/authorize/state/graph — no diff or apply command exists anywhere in the repo.","GDD staleness detection only fires for tasks that already have a committed evidence record (current_conformance.py compares canon['sha256'] against current_canon_hash inside the record-evaluation loop). The other ~36 of 37 task contracts have no evidence yet, so a GDD edit that invalidates their acceptance criteria produces zero signal until someone manually reruns full reconciliation and manually diffs 37 files by hand.","Neither live provider adapter (Claude or Codex) supports repository_write or approved_command_execution — the elaborate AgentRuntime/TaskExecution stack cannot currently make a single Unity code change, autonomously or semi-autonomously.","Evidence records require hand-authored JSON with exact Git blob SHA-256 values per conformance surface and gate artifact (CONFORMANCE_RECORDS.md), but no generator/authoring tool exists in Pipeline/TaskGraph — only a validator/reader (conformance_records.py exposes shape validation and load_committed_records, nothing that computes and writes a record).","The project's own accepted correction direction (CURRENT_STATE.md, 'Deferred Until Evidence Justifies It') explicitly warns against building infrastructure ahead of a proven single delivery loop, yet the five most recent commits (Stage 4A-4D) are all infrastructure for ArchitectureReview provider migration, not gameplay work — the project is not currently following its own stated rule."],"observed_failure_solutions":["Prior architecture review found mutable task 'status' was being treated as completion truth; Phase 1-3 replaced it with schema-2.0 contracts plus a separate evidence-derived conformance evaluator that reads only committed Git state.","Assignment 6 found a Refiner could report 'implemented' while making no actual file changes; ADR-016 makes a no-op refinement count as a failed repair attempt against budget.","Assignment 6 found static/source-level evaluation passed while the camera was unusable at runtime; ADR-015 makes runtime Unity evidence able to fail a task even after static evaluation passes.","An early Phase 3A test found uncommitted evidence could be mistaken for proof; the evaluator was built/verified to ignore working-tree state and only trust committed HEAD (demonstrated concretely with NSC-023)."],"hypothetical_failure_solutions":["Extensive provider trust-boundary adversarial hardening (malformed/duplicate JSON keys, NaN/Infinity rejection, path traversal in raw_log_reference, provider identity mismatch checks) defends against attacks that have not occurred in this single-user, offline, Docker-contained environment.","Git-blob-SHA-level integrity checking on every conformance surface and gate-artifact evidence record defends against evidence tampering that has never been observed and is unlikely given ADR-038's accepted single-trusted-user boundary.","Dual-provider (Claude vs Codex) architecture-review scaffolding, provider namespace separation, and 'later comparison' plumbing were built with 'no comparison pipeline exists yet' explicitly acknowledged — infrastructure for a feature that doesn't exist and has no scheduled owner.","ADR-027's two-different-model bootstrap verification requirement and the parallel multi-model verification crew (opus+sonnet, randomized model assignment, union-not-vote findings) is heavy machinery for a one-time 37-record bootstrap that has already happened and is marked 'do not rerun.'"],"overengineering":["Stage 4A-4D provider-adapter migration effort (turn-budget translation formulas, StandardProcessRunner, capability-mapping ADRs, provider registry identity checks) was spent entirely on migrating the ArchitectureReview meta-tool, which produces no game content and was already functional before the migration.","The evidence-record schema (delivery/baseline/revalidation with basis-chain ancestry cycle detection, Git blob SHA binding for every surface and artifact) is more rigorous than anything needed to prove one prototype scene works, and currently has no authoring tool, making it a burden rather than leverage for the next real task.","Immutable per-run reconciliation/verification directory trees with nested pass1/pass2/stream_repairs/MODEL_ASSIGNMENTS artifacts represent significant process ceremony for a single 37-item bootstrap that ran once."],"missing_components":["A GDD-change-to-task-contract impact/diff tool (promised, never built).","Any tool to author Phase 3A evidence records (compute Git blob SHAs, assemble the JSON) instead of hand-writing them.","Repository write capability in any provider adapter — without this, AgentRuntime cannot be used to implement anything.","ExecutionCrew (Planner/Implementer/Validator wired to AgentRuntime) — Assignment 3's crew and Assignment 6's GER loop remain isolated coursework, never integrated into the production runtime.","A cheap, per-task GDD-chunk hash/version binding at the task-contract level (contracts store free-text gdd_evidence references but no hash), so drift can only be detected after evidence already exists."],"state_and_authority_concerns":["AgentRuntime/TaskExecution separation (ADR-039) is a reasonable boundary in principle but currently guards a system with no real task-execution consumer; the split's value is unproven.","Tasks/*.yaml is declared 'approved definition of work, not completion truth,' and Phase 3A evidence is declared the completion authority — this two-tier model is coherent, but there is no defined authority for a third state that will matter constantly under an iterative GDD: 'this approved task definition may now be wrong because canon changed underneath it before any evidence was ever recorded.' Nothing owns that question today.","Reconciliation is correctly kept from directly mutating the graph, but because the promised diff/apply boundary doesn't exist, there is currently no path at all — not even a manual one with tool support — from a new reconciliation snapshot into the living graph after bootstrap."],"gdd_iteration_concerns":["The architecture treats GDD sync as binary: either nothing happens (silent drift) or a full multi-model reconciliation + verification crew re-runs (the same heavyweight bootstrap machinery), with no built middle tier for 'this one paragraph changed, which 2 tasks does it touch.'","Staleness detection is evidence-record-scoped, not contract-scoped, so the 36 of 37 tasks without evidence get no automated signal when GDD text they depend on changes.","CURRENT_STATE.md explicitly defers 'automatic GDD impact analysis without a reviewed causal model' to 'later candidates driven by observed production needs' — but the prompt's premise (GDD will keep changing while the game is built) makes this a near-certain near-term need, not a speculative one; deferring it risks accumulating undetected canon drift across most of the graph."],"throughput_assessment":"Zero gameplay features have been delivered through the pipeline's own machinery. The only Unity code that exists (15 C# files under one DoorPrototype scene: camera, door interaction, mana, health, WASD movement) was built directly by a human/Assignment coursework, not via AgentRuntime/TaskExecution/ExecutionCrew — none of which can currently write code at all. The one conformance proof (NSC-023) is a retrofit of pre-existing work into the new evidence schema, not a demonstration of the pipeline producing new work. All claimed leverage is still theoretical.","human_intervention_points":["Every reconciliation bootstrap and future reconciliation delta requires human approval before seeding/changing the graph.","NSC-003 cannot proceed without a human first resolving input-ownership/arbitration questions (click-to-move vs held-pointer, suspend/reset semantics) that CURRENT_STATE.md lists as open.","Every Phase 3A evidence record currently requires a human to hand-author JSON with exact Git blob SHAs (no tool exists).","Every task remains permanently gated by taskcontrol authorize returning DENIED — a human must manually drive every step of every task indefinitely under current policy.","Human Play Mode approval was required and recorded for NSC-023's only real conformance proof."],"next_slice":{"title":"Execute exactly one small NSC-003-derived gameplay slice by hand-in-the-loop with Claude, and build only the evidence-authoring tool this exposes as missing","why":"The architecture has never been exercised end-to-end on new work. The single highest-value experiment is not more AgentRuntime/provider plumbing but proving (or disproving) that the existing evidence/conformance model is usable in practice for a real, small, human-supervised delivery, since the pipeline cannot yet write code autonomously anyway.","deliverables":["Human resolves the NSC-003 input-ownership questions already listed in CURRENT_STATE.md and, if warranted, splits NSC-003 into a smaller first contract (e.g. just the shared pointer-projection foundation).","Implement that one small piece directly with Claude Code (interactive, human-supervised, no AgentRuntime dependency since write capability doesn't exist) and get it merged to main with Unity Play Mode evidence.","Build a minimal script (e.g. `taskcontrol record`) that computes Git blob SHAs and writes a schema-valid delivery/baseline evidence record instead of hand-authoring JSON.","Run `taskcontrol state` to prove the new task flips to conformant, and note exactly what broke or was missing along the way."],"proof_of_value":"A second real task (beyond NSC-023) reaches 'conformant' through the evidence model with materially less manual JSON authoring than today, and the exercise produces a concrete, evidence-based list of what ExecutionCrew/AgentRuntime write-capability work is actually needed next — rather than more speculative provider/transport investment."},"do_not_build_yet":["ExecutionCrew role orchestration or any autonomous dispatch/readiness policy.","Repository-write capability for provider adapters until at least one human-supervised task has proven the evidence loop end-to-end by hand.","Dual-provider (Claude vs Codex) comparison pipeline.","Milestone 2's full RAG/Scanner/Progressive-Decomposer/Artifact-Authority bundle as one platform — the project's own CURRENT_STATE.md already reaches this conclusion and it should be honored, not just documented.","Any further ArchitectureReview/AgentRuntime provider-migration refactoring; this tooling already works and does not block game progress."],"alternative_architecture":{"needed":false,"description":"The state/authority shape (deterministic graph, evidence-derived conformance, immutable audit trail, human merge gate, bounded worker) does not need to be replaced. If anything, a leaner version would drop the multi-provider transport abstraction and Git-blob-level evidence integrity until a single provider has actually delivered several real tasks through it.","why_better":"Not applicable — replacement is not warranted; the fix is sequencing (build write capability and lightweight GDD-drift detection before further governance hardening), not a different architecture."},"evidence":[{"path":"Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md","observation":"taskcontrol ready is hard-coded UNAVAILABLE and authorize is DENIED; no gameplay task has passed through the pipeline; ExecutionCrew, dependency readiness, and dispatch remain unimplemented."},{"path":"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py","observation":"build_parser only registers validate/list/show/ready/authorize/state/graph subcommands; no diff or apply command exists despite Reconciliation/README.md promising one."},{"path":"Pipeline/Reconciliation/README.md","observation":"States a 'deterministic taskcontrol reconciliation-diff/apply workflow will own that comparison in Milestone 1,' but Milestone 1 is marked complete and this tool was never built."},{"path":"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py","observation":"GDD/canon staleness (needs_revalidation) is only checked inside the per-record evaluation loop, so contracts without any evidence record get no staleness signal at all."},{"path":"Pipeline/AgentRuntime/providers/claude_code.py","observation":"_validate_request_policy rejects repository_write and approved_command_execution outright; the provider can only read/search, never write code."},{"path":"Pipeline/TaskExecution/README.md","observation":"TaskExecution only publishes audit data and delegates to AgentRuntime; explicitly states it does not establish delivery, readiness, authorization, or completion, and ExecutionCrew remains outside this layer."},{"path":"Pipeline/TaskGraph/CONFORMANCE_RECORDS.md and conformance_records.py","observation":"Evidence records require hand-specified Git blob SHA-256 values per surface/artifact; conformance_records.py exposes only shape validation/loading, no authoring tool."},{"path":"Glob: Assets/**/*.cs vs Pipeline infra tree","observation":"Only 15 gameplay C# files exist (one DoorPrototype scene) versus dozens of Python modules across TaskGraph, AgentRuntime, Reconciliation, ArchitectureReview, and TaskExecution."},{"path":"Docs/AI-Pipeline/START_HERE.md","observation":"'The next infrastructure work should also advance a real No Safe Circle task rather than creating another infrastructure-only stretch' — yet the five most recent commits (Stage 4A-4D) are ArchitectureReview provider migration, not gameplay work."}],"confidence":0.72,"biggest_uncertainty":"Whether the team intends the very next session (post-checkpoint) to pivot hard into executing NSC-003-derived work by hand, which would resolve most of my throughput concerns quickly, or whether momentum will continue toward further AgentRuntime/ExecutionCrew infrastructure (e.g., adding write capability, building ExecutionCrew) before any second real task is proven through the evidence model — I could not observe intent beyond the frozen commit."},"ttft_ms":6956,"ttft_stream_ms":6385,"time_to_request_ms":5758,"type":"result","duration_ms":267664,"uuid":"1871f1db-636d-40c4-a734-71bd68a1f971"}
